<title>USA: Marathon raises U.S. posted crude prices.</title>
<headline>Marathon raises U.S. posted crude prices.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon said it raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 50 cents a barrel, effective September 27.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $23 a barrel, and West Texas Sour to $21.40 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $23 a barrel, and Oklahoma sweet is $23.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859-1620</p>
</text>
